{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1182653-hillfolk-the-desperation-a-fan-game-open-development-thread","id":1182653,"title":"Hillfolk: The Desperation-A Fan Game (Open Development Thread)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-05T10:59:02-08:00","id":1182653,"title":"Hillfolk: The Desperation-A Fan Game (Open Development Thread)","content":"Alright, I have decided I want to make a fan game for the New World of Darkness/Chronicles of Darkness, specifically the First Edition rules set, as I personally do not care for CofD Second Edition (mainly for mechanical reasons) and I am more familiar with 1E anyway so I am going to try and work within those parameters. However, if any of you want to adapt this idea for Second Edition, be my guest.<br /> <br /> The fan game I have in mind is a New World of Darkness take on the &quot;Hixploitation&quot; genre of horror where hapless suburban city-dwellers wander into the wilderness and are attacked by backwoods savages. It's a well-known horror cliche that has been seen in many works such as Fallout 3's <i>Point Lookout</i> DLC, <i>Deliverance</i>, <i>The Hills Have Eyes</i>, <i>Wrong Turn</i>, and too many others to list. The parody horror film <i>Tucker &amp; Dale vs. Evil</i> is an excellent deconstruction of the genre.<br /> <br /> A little bit of background on the concept and why I want to make this into a game: I grew up in the rural hills of Central Appalachia, specifically the coalfields of Southwestern Virginia (Dickenson County, VA and Wise County, VA) and believe me, I am intimately familiar with the stereotypes and cliches of my people, and the Hixploitation genre has not helped at all. However, I want to take the genre and turn it on its head. Essentially I'm taking the tired &quot;backwoods redneck savages&quot; cliche and &quot;taking it back&quot;, so to speak. By making the so-called savage backwoods monsters playable and somewhat sympathetic, I am lending an alternate point of view on the genre.<br /> <br /> The main themes of <i>Hillfolk: The Desperation </i>are honor, desperate survivalism, tribalism, distrust of outsiders, and solemn duties of holding back ancient and eldritch evils, even if it means taking extreme and desperate actions. I want to have sort of a cosmic horror bent to it, almost Lovecraftian, as if the Hillfolk are trying to hold back some sort of eldritch monstrosity. The game draws heavily on themes established in the Classic WoD games <i>Werewolf: The Apocalypse </i>and <i>Hunter: The Reckoning. </i><br /> <br /> The Players are rustic outcasts known as Hillfolk, regardless of where they are from. The Hillfolk are those imbued or cursed with ancient powers and markings to defend mankind from a collection of ancient and unfathomable horrors known as The Outsiders, whose motives are unknowable and generally destructive. Some of the Hillfolk were once normal humans cursed by The Outsiders while others were born into their unfortunate state. Some Hillfolk look outwardly deformed or mutated by these curses, while others are insane. Yet others may appear to be of &quot;normal&quot; mind and body, but are damaged spiritually. These same curses also have left them open to powers granted to them by mysterious beings known as The Enlightened, designating these unfortunate few to go into the far reaches of wilderness and make war against The Outsiders, whether it be to save the world, save their hometown, or just save their own souls. <br /> <br /> I want this game to be more in the open-ended toolkit style of the early First Edition releases, so there will be five main splats and possibly five faction splats as well. This game is in the very early development phases and it is an open development thread where anyone can offer input on it.<br /> <br /> There would be five splats called &quot;Families&quot;, equivalent to Vampire Clans or Werewolf Auspices. I have yet to determine the exact names, archetypes, and powers of each Family, but the premise is there. So far, I have the following ideas for Families....<br /> <br /> A Family centered around defending sacred places or keeping outsiders away from lands where no human should dare tread.<br /> <br /> A Family centered around hunting down and slaying the servants of The Outsiders, many of whom are scouts, spies, and trackers.<br /> <br /> A Family centered around preserving ancient rituals and traditions, often scavenging for ancient relics to ward off The Outsiders.<br /> <br /> A Family of rugged survivalists who realize that The Outsiders will rise up, but they will do their best to endure and rebuild from the ashes.<br /> <br /> A Family of warlike and militant hillfolk who want to confront The Outsiders and their servants directly and hopefully win the war.<br /> <br /> Again, this is in the very early stages of development and I just came up with the idea this morning, but I felt it was too good to let go and so I decided to share the idea and from here, develop it further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T18:27:59-07:00","id":1198481,"title":"","content":"This sounds kind of similar to my <br /> Guardians: The Elusive idea I had that was playing as Sasquatch/Bigfoot/Yeti entities who were actually ancient guardians that would travel through a series of interconnected portals serving as guardians to areas of eldritch connection to keep whatever was in contained. A lot of my inspiration coming from the book, The Haunted Mesa","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T18:36:06-07:00","id":1198489,"title":"","content":"So are they mutated/tainted so that if they breed with other humans their children inherit the deformity, or do you have a kind of latent level of kinship like Wolfblooded, or latent psychics?<br /> <br /> What type of powers? We have physical mutations and enhancement, but do they have their own magic like Houdoo?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T18:39:04-07:00","id":1198492,"title":"","content":"As for this though, maybe instead of families it's based more on geographical areas like<br /> <br /> Mountain-Men: just like they sound, big strong men from the mountains, especially around Appalachia.<br /> <br /> Swamp-Rats: gator wrestling Cajuns sometimes Brutish and sometimes clever, always craftier than people give them credit for. They watch over the great bayous and swamps<br /> <br /> Woodsmen: dwell in the thick unsettled great forests, living hand to mouth off the land and watching over what lurks in the untamed forests<br /> <br /> Desert folk: they live in the hills and caverns around places like Arizona and New Mexico, in and out in a flash like they were never there. They watch over what lurks in the sand<br /> <br /> Longshoremen: Often found in isolated fishing villages or old port towns with no one in them, sort of inspired by the citizens of innsmouth, they watch over what lurks in the sea","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T18:45:04-07:00","id":1198495,"title":"","content":"Mountain men are the physical or maybe the more leadership inclined, Swamp rats with their Cajun roots can be like the voodoo/houdoo ones, woodsmen are like stealthy classic hunters or could be more physical, longshoremen might be the most connected with society as they still live in areas that have ports and docks, and the desert folk the stealthy ones","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T18:48:13-07:00","id":1198497,"title":"","content":"Or these would be the &quot;Auspices&quot; and the families would be like the &quot;Tribes&quot; to borrow werewolf terms<br /> <br /> Maybe call it &quot;Heritage&quot; for the Auspice and &quot;Clan&quot; for the Tribe<br /> <br /> That or reverse Clan and Heritage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13063,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","user":"Lord Jub-Jub","date":". 03-22-2018, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T19:36:30-07:00","id":1198512,"title":"","content":"Or you could have Families as organizations that you are born/wed into, and something for your preferred local like Dwelling, and maybe one more like Inheritance for your mutations/taint.<br /> <br /> Maybe they are tied to their dwellings, and the Families have a strong proclivity towards living in a Holler, or the Hills but there are outliers in the families who live elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T19:44:14-07:00","id":1198516,"title":"","content":"Though I wonder if they are sufficiently different from vanilla mortals to be considered a splat in and of themselves, generally speaking I would say if they still use integrity(or morality in this case since its 1E) they are still human essentially and may only be a quasi-splat like a wolf blooded or ghoul. Having a mutation or deformity doesn't make one not human, and there are plenty of mortals who have supernatural powers to a degree. Even Slashers still used morality(with freaks and mutants partially representing the hillbilly horrors of pop culture) they just had low to no morality. This could be better represented as a mystery cult, or a hunter like compact. Or as I said before, more of a Quasi-Splat<br /> <br /> Maybe even repurpose slashers into them to a degree, just alter it a bit so they don't have to be murderous psychos. Using slasher undertakings like brute and freak primarily though I could see arguments for avenger, genius and charmer","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13063,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","user":"Lord Jub-Jub","date":". 03-22-2018, 10:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T20:40:34-07:00","id":1198534,"title":"","content":"While I am all about doing better ChroD/WoD material for Appalachia (its almost becoming a personal brand at this point), I'm not sure if doing an entire splat is the best approach. For one, while &quot;mutant hillbilly&quot; is definitely a well worn trope it's a little hard to translate into a splat (in my opinion at least) because of the difficulty of disentangling the &quot;mutant&quot; part from the &quot;hillbilly&quot; part. Are they a splat because they're mutants? If so then the focus becomes much more about the mutation than about their being from them thar hills. On the other hand if they are a splat because they are hillbillies then while that does preserve the desired focus it does create some awkward and potentially problematic implications. I definitely understand wanting to reclaim stereotypes, but I'm not necessarily all about starting that from the position that these &quot;Hillfolk&quot; are in actuality a species of supernatural beings distinct and apart from humanity. <br /> <br /> To be clear: I'm not nay-saying the entire idea. I like several of the concepts presented, but I think that there may be better ways to express them than through a splat-game. Honestly if people wanted to collaborate on some kind of broader Night Horrors or other blue book type supplement focused on Appalachia that is something I'd definitely be down for.<br /> <br /> For my own part, background-wise: I spent the first twenty five years of my life (which is to say all but the last five) bouncing around between parts of WV and southwestern PA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T20:52:44-07:00","id":1198539,"title":"","content":"A lot can be done to convince this is a splat by doing footwork on the Chthonic beings that dwell in the Land and lend themselves to the legends of these splats. So they become something like a Bloodborne splat. Like maybe they are not just great old ones but they are the future of a highly evolved humanity from the end of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T07:29:49-07:00","id":1198640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1182653-hillfolk-the-desperation-a-fan-game-open-development-thread#post1182653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There would be five splats called &quot;Families&quot;, equivalent to Vampire Clans or Werewolf Auspices. I have yet to determine the exact names, archetypes, and powers of each Family, but the premise is there. So far, I have the following ideas for Families....<br /> <br /> A Family centered around defending sacred places or keeping outsiders away from lands where no human should dare tread.<br /> <br /> A Family centered around hunting down and slaying the servants of The Outsiders, many of whom are scouts, spies, and trackers.<br /> <br /> A Family centered around preserving ancient rituals and traditions, often scavenging for ancient relics to ward off The Outsiders.<br /> <br /> A Family of rugged survivalists who realize that The Outsiders will rise up, but they will do their best to endure and rebuild from the ashes.<br /> <br /> A Family of warlike and militant hillfolk who want to confront The Outsiders and their servants directly and hopefully win the war.<br /> <br /> Again, this is in the very early stages of development and I just came up with the idea this morning, but I felt it was too good to let go and so I decided to share the idea and from here, develop it further.</div> </div> </div> </div>These sound more like covenant and tribe analogues than clan or auspice. For the Families, I would suggest something describing how they're cursed or damaged: maybe call it their Marks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T07:52:08-07:00","id":1198657,"title":"","content":"Maybe take a cue from Promethean (i.e. other created, not just Frankenstein) and see if there are other similar stories from around the world that can be used to fill out the game. Then you could have the x splat be the origin and the y be there purpose","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T07:53:25-07:00","id":1198658,"title":"","content":"For me the best way to visualize these things is to look at a character sheet and have it explained piece by piece. So here's my drafts of a character sheet<br /> <br /> Name: <br /> Dwelling: <br /> Clan: <br /> Vice: <br /> Virtue: <br /> Harmony: <br /> <br /> Gumption: 1<br /> <br /> Size: 5<br /> Speed: <br /> Defense: <br /> Initiative: <br /> Armor: 0/0<br /> Health: <br /> Willpower: <br /> Moxie: <br /> <br /> Attributes: 5/4/3<br /> Intelligence 1<br /> Wits 1<br /> Resolve 1<br /> <br /> Strength 1<br /> Dexterity 1<br /> Stamina 1<br /> <br /> Presence 1<br /> Manipulation 1<br /> Composure 1<br /> <br /> Skills: 11/7/4<br /> <br /> Specialties: 3<br /> <br /> Merits: 10<br /> <br /> Inheritances<br /> <br /> *<br /> *<br /> *<br /> Dwelling would be what type of Hillfolk they are, similar to a bloodline or auspice. Keeping to the model of 5 we have<br /> <br /> Mountain-Men: Living up in isolated mountain ranges, such as the Appalachia area but could also represent something similar to Gurkhas, characterized by being physically powerful typically<br /> <br /> Backwoodsmen: Living out in the woods, hunting, trapping and fishing to live off the land. They are heavily inclined towards the survivalist archetype.<br /> <br /> Swamp-Rats: Whether Hoodoo witch doctors or gator punchers, these are the ones that live in the bayous and swamps. They don't have to be Cajun though, witch doctors living in the swamps are an old stereotype from all over the world<br /> <br /> Bushmen: living out in the deserts and plains, they know the tunnels and caverns inside and out, associated with aboriginal Australians, Native Americans and Steppe Riders, Bushmen are the historical raiders in and out in a flash<br /> <br /> Longshoremen: inspired by the citizens of Dunwich and Innsmouth, these are the citizens of the coastal rural towns that Lovecraft was so critical of. Whether Massachusetts, Maine or even the British Isles, the stereotype of the sea faring locals suspicious of outlanders is common.<br /> <br /> Clans would be the organizations Hillfolk ally themselves with, these would be the families you spoke of, with their goals being what you wrote<br /> <br /> I didn't know exactly what they would use for morality, but in my experience many of these stereotypes take a pride in being one with the land, and Prometheans and Vampires already share humanity so maybe use Harmony for these guys<br /> <br /> Gumption is the power stat, the analogue to Blood Potency or Primal Urge.<br /> <br /> Moxie, I gotta be honest, I just didn't know what their Vitae/Essence analogue would be so I just kind of made it up<br /> <br /> Inheritances would be the special powers, like werewolf Gifts and Vampire Disciplines, the inheritances you get partially determined by Dwelling and Clan.<br /> <br /> Other Notes<br /> The party name for a group of Hillfolk(like pack for werewolves or cabal for mages) is A Holler<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what kind of special anchors they'd have, and I'm still iffy on the Harmony and Moxie thing, we'd have to come up some base powers but I can't think of any right now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}